    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Born and raised in Stratford-upon-Avon, Shakespeare was a known figure in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> by 1592 and became an actor, writer and part-owner of the leading playing company, which gave him a large estate.</li><li>He wrote comedies and histories in the 1590s, mainly tragedies until 1608 and romances in his last phase, and appears to have retired to Stratford around 1613, three years before his death.</li><li>Few records of his private life survive, so his religion, his sexuality and his appearance have been argued over, and his friends Heminges and Condell published his plays in the First Folio of 1623.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Globe burned to the ground on 29 June 1613 when a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cannon">cannon</a> fired during a performance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a> set fire to the thatch, an event that pinpoints the date of a Shakespeare play with rare precision.</p></aside>
    </section>

